  "details": "Currently, VRChat’s microphone processing seems heavily optimized for speech, which causes major issues when using a mic for music (e.g., playing piano live).\n\nWhen I play piano into my mic:\n\n- The sound becomes metallic and distorted\n\n- Compression removes most of the dynamics\n\n- Noise suppression and processing make it sound unnatural\n\nEven with a good microphone and proper setup, the audio ends up sounding very degraded.\n\nSUGGESTION:\n\nIt would be really helpful to have a high-fidelity microphone mode or an option that reduces audio processing, for example:\n\n- Lower or disabled compression\n\n- Reduced/no noise suppression\n\n- Higher bitrate audio for better sound quality\n\nThis could be:\n\n- A toggle in settings (opt-in, since it may use more bandwidth), or\n\n- A per-user permission/role\n\nALTERNATIVE IDEA:\n\n- A special role (e.g., “Music/Mic Quality” role) that users can apply for (possibly via Discord or moderation)\n\n- This role would allow access to higher-quality microphone transmission\n\n- Useful for musicians performing live (piano, vocals, instruments)\n\nThis wouldn’t affect normal voice chat but would allow people who want to share music to do so without the audio being heavily degraded.\n\nThanks for considering this!",
